+---
+id: dl-005-createpatch-emits-a-minimal-recursive-diff-arrays-compared-by-index
+type: decision-log
+title: "createPatch emits a minimal recursive diff, arrays compared by index"
+status: pending
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+## Context
+Clients want to send only the change between two document versions as a JSON Patch.
+
+## Decision
+Recursive diff: objects member by member, arrays index by index (trailing `remove`s in descending
+order, trailing `add`s ascending), any other difference is one `replace` at that path. No `move`/`copy`
+detection and no LCS array alignment. Output order follows member insertion order, so it is deterministic.
+Non-JSON inputs throw, like `applyMergePatch`.
+
+## Consequences
+Patches are small for local changes and always correct. Inserting at the front of a long array yields
+many operations (not the shortest possible patch); an LCS-based diff can be adopted later without changing the API.
